{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":398,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","line":827,"source":"\\begin{definition}[covariant derivative of an $(s,t)$-tensor field]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0075}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection}\n\n  For an $(s,t)$-tensor field $S$, the \\emph{covariant derivative} $\\nabla S$\n  is the $(s,t+1)$-tensor field determined by requiring the Leibniz rule\n  $\\nabla_X(S(Y))=(\\nabla_XS)(Y)+S(\\nabla_XY)$: for $s=0,1$,\n  \\[\n    \\nabla S(X,Y_1,\\dots,Y_r)=(\\nabla_XS)(Y_1,\\dots,Y_r)\n    =\\nabla_X\\big(S(Y_1,\\dots,Y_r)\\big)-\\sum_{i=1}^rS(Y_1,\\dots,\\nabla_XY_i,\\dots,Y_r),\n  \\]\n  where $\\nabla_X$ acts as $D_X$ on functions and as covariant differentiation\n  on vector fields; equivalently $\\nabla_XS=[\\nabla_X,S]$ when $S$ is\n  $(1,1)$. For general $s$, extend by the product rule\n  $\\nabla_X(X_1\\otimes X_2)=(\\nabla_XX_1)\\otimes X_2+X_1\\otimes(\\nabla_XX_2)$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[covariant derivative of an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(s,t)$\">$(s,t)$</span>-tensor field] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d636f76617269616e742d646572697661746976652d74656e736f72\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0075</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-riemannian-connection\">↗ def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection</a> <p></p>For an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(s,t)$\">$(s,t)$</span>-tensor field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span>, the <em>covariant derivative</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla S$\">$\\nabla S$</span> is the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(s,t+1)$\">$(s,t+1)$</span>-tensor field determined by requiring the Leibniz rule <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _X(S(Y))=(\\nabla _XS)(Y)+S(\\nabla _XY)$\">$\\nabla _X(S(Y))=(\\nabla _XS)(Y)+S(\\nabla _XY)$</span>: for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s=0,1$\">$s=0,1$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\nabla S(X,Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r)=(\\nabla _XS)(Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r) =\\nabla _X\\big(S(Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r)\\big)-\\sum _{i=1}^rS(Y_1,\\dots ,\\nabla _XY_i,\\dots ,Y_r),  \\]\">\\[  \\nabla S(X,Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r)=(\\nabla _XS)(Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r) =\\nabla _X\\big(S(Y_1,\\dots ,Y_r)\\big)-\\sum _{i=1}^rS(Y_1,\\dots ,\\nabla _XY_i,\\dots ,Y_r),  \\]</span> where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _X$\">$\\nabla _X$</span> acts as <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D_X$\">$D_X$</span> on functions and as covariant differentiation on vector fields; equivalently <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _XS=[\\nabla _X,S]$\">$\\nabla _XS=[\\nabla _X,S]$</span> when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(1,1)$\">$(1,1)$</span>. For general <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s$\">$s$</span>, extend by the product rule <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _X(X_1\\otimes X_2)=(\\nabla _XX_1)\\otimes X_2+X_1\\otimes (\\nabla _XX_2)$\">$\\nabla _X(X_1\\otimes X_2)=(\\nabla _XX_1)\\otimes X_2+X_1\\otimes (\\nabla _XX_2)$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-normal-coordinates-frame","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-parallel-tensor","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","title":"def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection","label":"def:pet-ch2-riemannian-connection"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-parallel-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch2-parallel-tensor","label":"def:pet-ch2-parallel-tensor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-hessian-covariant-derivative","title":"prop:pet-ch2-hessian-covariant-derivative","label":"prop:pet-ch2-hessian-covariant-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity","title":"prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity","label":"prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-exterior-derivative-covariant","title":"def:pet-ch2-exterior-derivative-covariant","label":"def:pet-ch2-exterior-derivative-covariant"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-second-covariant-derivative","title":"def:pet